+# Updating existing results
+
+Updating existing results is most helpful if you are writing a `shiny` or other
+user interface for PKNCA. If you are using PKNCA from a script, this is not the
+preferred way to perform analysis.
+
+If you need to rerun analyses with minor updates-- changing half-life point
+selection, for instance-- you can use `update()` on a `PKNCAresults` object
+(`o_nca` in the example above). Using `update()` will recalculate the
+minimum-required number of calculations for the data that are changed.
+
+To use `update()`, give it your existing results and the new `PKNCAdata` object
+you want to use.
+
+Starting from the theophylline example in the [Quick Start](Quick Start) section above:
+
+```{r update-example-setup}
+d_conc <- as.data.frame(datasets::Theoph)
+d_dose <- d_conc[d_conc$Time == 0,]
+o_conc <- PKNCAconc(d_conc, conc~Time|Subject)
+o_dose <- PKNCAdose(d_dose, Dose~Time|Subject)
+o_data <- PKNCAdata(o_conc, o_dose)
+o_nca <- pk.nca(o_data)
+summary(o_nca)
+```
+
+In these data, some participants have a nonzero predose concentration. Assume
+that we want to manually change those concentrations to zero and then
+recalculate. You can change the concentration data, and use `update()` to
+recalculate only for the changed participants.
+
+```{r update-example-setzero}
+d_conc_setzero <- as.data.frame(datasets::Theoph)
+d_conc_setzero$conc[d_conc$Time == 0] <- 0
+o_conc_update <- PKNCAconc(d_conc_setzero, conc~Time|Subject)
+o_data_update <- PKNCAdata(o_conc_update, o_dose)
+o_nca_update <- update(o_nca, o_data_update)
+summary(o_nca_update)
+```
+
+Now, assume that instead of calculating `auclast` from time 0 to 24, we want to
+calculate `aucint.inf.obs`. We can change the intervals to create a new
+`PKNCAdata` object:
+
+```{r update-example-newdata}
+d_intervals <- o_data$intervals
+d_intervals$aucint.inf.obs <- d_intervals$auclast
+d_intervals$auclast <- FALSE
+o_data_update <- PKNCAdata(o_conc, o_dose, intervals = d_intervals)
+```
+
+Then, we can update the `PKNCAresults`:
+
+```{r update-example-complete}
+o_nca_update <- update(o_nca, o_data_update)
+summary(o_nca_update)
+```
